{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED. Gerrit change 2070 merged as e795f5521cf49094fccef565878194f0453a7c1a on main\n(Change-Id I5d0a03b5354ac692a1c906ef453cff97ad9a7f0c; Gerrit rebased on submit, so the\nmerged sha differs from the locally authored 4ca6d11831f).\n\nVOTES\n  LLM-Review +1  [LLM-Review: PASS] rebar code review passed, 2 ADVISORY comments,\n                 both already marked resolved (unresolved_comment_count = 0):\n                 (a) maintainability: the guard keys on the literal 'os.O_CREAT', so a\n                     fourth copy using 'from os import O_CREAT' would evade it. Kept as\n                     is: that literal IS the anchor AC 1 mandates, and it is load-bearing\n                     -- a bare 'O_CREAT' match re-introduces the doctor_locks false\n                     positive the plan rejected in EXPERIMENT 2, because doctor_locks\n                     says 'O_CREAT' in prose at :119 without the 'os.' prefix.\n                 (b) tests: the O_EXCL survivor counts include docstring prose and so are\n                     brittle to unrelated doc edits. Kept: that count IS AC 2.\n  Verified +1    GitHub Actions run 32554584200, all jobs green (lint+typecheck, pytest on\n                 ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos py3.13, pip-audit, optionality,\n                 mutation-shard select, artifact provenance, eval discipline, golden path,\n                 authorship gate). No recheck was needed; the de95 fsck flake did not fire.\n\nPER-AC EVIDENCE (all seven, verified on the merged tree at e795f5521cf)\n  1. No module outside stamped_lock.py performs the acquire.\n     grep -rlF 'os.O_CREAT' src/rebar --include='*.py' | xargs grep -lF\n       'stamped_file_is_stale' | grep -v '^src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py$'\n     -> prints NOTHING (it printed all three copies before the change), and\n     pytest tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py -q -> 20 passed.\n  2. The unrelated O_EXCL uses survive: grep -c over keyprov.py, code_review/registry.py,\n     _signing_hmac.py, _store/fsutil.py, doctor_locks.py -> 1+1+2+1+2 = 7, unchanged.\n  3. The six lock functions are still module attributes with unchanged signatures:\n     test_enrich_drain + test_compact_trigger + test_lock_holder_labelling +\n     test_lock_age_ceiling + test_snapshot_gc_trigger + tests/unit/store +\n     test_doctor_dirty_tree -> 148 passed, with NO assertion edited. The two\n     monkeypatch.setattr sites at test_lock_holder_labelling.py:134-135 still resolve.\n  4. The stamp is .strip()-equal to lock_owner._owner_stamp() and doctor resolves a holder\n     from a lock made through the helper:\n     test_the_stamp_is_strip_equal_and_doctor_resolves_a_holder_from_it (drives the real\n     doctor_locks._existence_report and asserts holder['pid']).\n  5. Releasing a lock whose os.close raises still unlinks:\n     test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails. This is the behaviour CHANGE to the drain,\n     not a preserved behaviour -- the drain previously leaked the lock for up to 3600 s.\n  6. The drain's reclaim WARNING still names the holder: _describe_drain_lock_holder is\n     injected as describe_holder, and\n     test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically passes unchanged.\n  7. Net non-test LOC is negative: git show --numstat HEAD -- src/rebar -> -2 on the merged\n     (rebased) commit, -6 as authored.\n\nMETHOD: held-out TDD. 20 tests authored first; RED was 17 failed / 3 passed, every failure\nModuleNotFoundError for rebar._store.stamped_lock (the 3 passes are deliberate invariance\npins). 18 edge/guard/E2E tests were then held OUT of the tree while the implementation was\nwritten against the 2 happy-path tests alone; the full set was restored unchanged and went\ngreen. Mutation: re-introducing the one-try release form killed exactly\ntest_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails, and an ast walk confirmed the mutant had 1\nexecutable try-block in release_stamped_lock versus 2 restored -- i.e. the mutation hit\ncode, not a docstring copy of the same literal.\n\nRESIDUAL, recorded not fixed: the guard's evasion path in advisory comment (a) above. It is\na deliberate consequence of the anchor the plan chose after two rejected experiments."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787379139763222001,"uuid":"1287f6a3-3e9c-4d89-b3c6-cc1a6a699c61"}